# core.autocrlf=true on Windows would check these out with CRLF, which breaks
# them on Linux: bash fails on a `\r` in a shebang or command, and Docker
# carries the `\r` into RUN lines. Everything here executes in a container or
# on a CI runner, so pin them to LF regardless of platform.
# The catch-all replaces a list of extensions that missed *.json and *.js, so a
# Windows checkout left package.json and package-lock.json looking modified from
# inside the devcontainer — line-ending noise that buries real changes.
* text=auto eol=lf
